native_ros2_messages
    The Rust message types in the `native_ros2_messages` crate are generated at
    build time from the ROS 2 `.msg` interface definitions vendored under
    `crates/native_ros2_messages/msg/`. The generated Rust code is part of
    Cerulion and is licensed under AGPL-3.0-only. The vendored `.msg`
    definitions stay under their own upstream licenses, which are not all the
    same license.

    Every vendored package is listed below with its upstream repository, the
    revision recorded for it in
    `crates/native_ros2_messages/upstream_msg_manifest.txt`, and the exact
    value its upstream `package.xml` gives in the `<license>` element at that
    revision. A copyright holder is named only where upstream states one.

    The same list, with the BSD-3-Clause text beside it, also ships inside the
    crate as `msg/README.md`, so a copy of the definitions obtained from the
    published crate carries the notice the BSD terms require.

